  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nThe weather pattern will stay relatively stagnant through the\nnext several days as high pressure maintains influence over the\nregion. This will result in dry weather through at least early\nnext week in addition to near normal temperatures. Highs will \nbe in the 60s with lows in the 30s and lower 40s each day, \nalthough temperatures may begin to warm towards the end of the \nweekend as the high starts to shift east. The only notable \nhazard over the next several days will be related to frost \npotential with efficient radiational cooling occurring most \nnights. That said, the best chance of frost will be in locations\nwhere the growing season has already ended. Will need to keep \nan eye on how temperatures trend in typical cold spots across \nWayne/Ashland/Holmes counties tonight into early Wednesday \nmorning, but there's potential for patchy fog (which may be\ndense in western zones) and lower stratus which could throw a \nwrench in radiational cooling/frost coverage in that area.",
